{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013pfFtZjMu8qzNw8r5ccgRS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc hr range \"%lthr\" start end Garmin export zone\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725?page=2\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/9\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725\"},{\"title\":\"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range\"},{\"title\":\"Running Workout Builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/running-workout-builder/5805\"},{\"title\":\"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521?page=9\"}]\n\nThe search turned up only community forum threads, not official intervals.icu documentation, so treat these as anecdotal.\n\n- **Zones resolve to a range, not a midpoint:** One forum reply says intervals.icu resolves zones to actual bpm values before sending workouts to Garmin or Suunto. The zone already defines a range, so a zone step sends its full low-to-high span. Settings ranges apply only to fixed steps. The ranges in settings are used for fixed steps.\n- **Percent-of-LTHR targets:** One user says the target HR is sent as % of LTHR, so mismatched LTHR values between the sending and receiving apps can produce wrong targets. A different user reported that Garmin-originated workouts showed bpm zones off by exactly 100 bpm in intervals.icu.\n- **Garmin 100-bpm workaround:** A developer reply says a fix was deployed. For Garmin-manufactured files only, if a custom HR range's high end is 80 or less after subtracting 100, the values are used as-is. This is only applied if the file manufacturer is Garmin.\n- **Zone steps by name:** A forum post says that at the moment you need to use percentage of LTHR or % of max HR for custom HR targets, which suggests zone-name steps were not yet supported when that was written. A later post describes adding support for zone-based HR steps, so this may be outdated.\n- **Custom HRR zones:** One user used Garmin's %HRR zones and recreated them in intervals.icu by entering percentages of LTHR. They also requested native %HRR (Karvonen) support, which suggests it is not built in. You can create Custom zones with any anchor you want.\n\nFor the exact `workout_doc` JSON fields and Garmin export behavior, check the official intervals.icu docs or API reference, which weren't in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c5bcb2c-62fd-4fcd-9aab-bb91e8cf1ee6","uuid":"415232a3-8425-4527-ac63-3032e7243d2f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:37:07.894Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc hr range \"%lthr\" start end Garmin export zone","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018aTB1Y1YDAdBD77u94HKUP","content":[{"title":"Building workout using zone number instead of per